==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[blood bath]]

===Etymology===
Coined in [[w:1867|1867]]. Compound of ''[[blood]]'' and ''[[bath]],'' the latter used to refer in the metaphorical sense to a [[deluge]] of a thing.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[blood]][[bath]]}}

# [[indiscriminate|Indiscriminate]] [[killing]] or [[slaughter]].
#* '''22 March 2012''', Scott Tobias, AV Club ''The Hunger Games''[http://www.avclub.com/articles/the-hunger-games,71293/]
#*: In movie terms, it suggests Paul Verhoeven in Robocop/Starship Troopers mode, an R-rated '''bloodbath''' where the grim spectacle of children murdering each other on television is bread-and-circuses for the age of reality TV, enforced by a totalitarian regime to keep the masses at bay. 
# {{figuratively}} An [[upset]] (as of a game with [[unexpected]] results.)

